havior generates correct (uniquified) Verilog. Reporter says "this may be surprising to a user" — i.e., behavior is arguably working as intended (uniquing handles it), and adding an error is an enhancement. Also correct behavior choice (error in LowerToHW vs annotation parsing vs allow) is a design decision. I'd say NOT_A_BUG (feature request), or at minimum UNCLEAR.

